<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Gottlieb Christaller</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1827–1895</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Gottlieb Christaller was a German missionary and linguist of the Basel Mission who worked on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>, now Ghana, from 1853. Based largely at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akropong">Akropong</a>, he translated the Bible into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akuapem-twi">Akuapem Twi</a>, completing it in 1871, and wrote a grammar and a large dictionary of the language. He also collected thousands of Twi proverbs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-gottlieb-christaller.jpg" alt="Johann Gottlieb Christaller" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown woodcutter of the late 19th century · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christaller_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
